Tasks: Phase 4 UI — statement upload, fee breakdown, reconciliation indicator
       (Phase 4, Tier 3)

WHAT CHANGED
  components/rental-payments-section.tsx (substantially rewritten)
  app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/(tabs)/rent/page.tsx

  - Per-row statement upload (hidden file input, driven by an upload button),
    a "Statement" link that fetches a signed URL on demand, and a remove action.
  - Fee breakdown as a secondary line under each payment: total fees, third
    party, other income, received, reconciliation status, confirmation status.
  - "Confirm fees" button, shown only when fees exist and are unconfirmed.
  - Dialog gains the four fee inputs, third-party outgoings, other income + note,
    and received — with a LIVE reconciliation readout as you type.
  - Section-level banners: how many statements await confirmation, and how many
    payments are flagged as possibly holding net rather than gross.
  - "Unverified" badge on rows carrying the NEEDS VERIFICATION marker written by
    scripts/fix-rental-payment-gross-net.ts.

COPY DECISIONS, which are the substance of this phase
  - The amount field is labelled "Gross rent", not "Amount", with help text
    saying it is the Money In total and NOT what reached the bank. The old label
    is how the wrong figure got entered in the first place.
  - Third-party outgoings says explicitly it is "not deducted here, because
    those costs are claimed from their own invoices" — the double-count guard
    stated where someone might otherwise assume the opposite.
  - The unconfirmed banner says what the consequence is: fees are not claimed and
    the pack falls back to the percentage estimate. A warning that does not say
    what it costs you gets ignored.
  - A failed reconciliation says "a balance brought forward can cause this. You
    can still save." Advisory, per FR5 — it never blocks.
  - Delete confirmation now warns that removing a payment "reduces the rental
    income reported for the year", and mentions the statement goes too.

REMOVED A TYPE ASSERTION
The rent page had `(supabase as any)` with an eslint-disable on the
rental_payments query. Per the style guide a cast around a Supabase query
usually means database.types.ts is stale rather than that the cast is right —
and that was the case: the table's types were incomplete before this track. Both
the cast and the `as unknown as RentalPayment[]` on the prop are gone, so the
query is now genuinely type-checked.

The component's RentalPayment type is now re-exported from
lib/supabase/database.types rather than hand-declared, so it cannot drift from
the row shape again.

